2. ACG Integration Team
-----------------------

- Responsible for ACG-specific integrations.
- Builds, customizes and maintains integrations based on ACG
  business requirements.
- Handles customized integrations required for ACG.
- Example: Payment Gateway integration.
- The team supports and maintains the integrations required
  for ACG applications.


3. Application Integration Team
-------------------------------

- Responsible for application-level integrations.
- The team is managed/maintained by Cognizant IT Services.
- Supports integrations between applications and external
  services.
- Address Sourcing was mentioned as one of the examples.
- The team also supports other application integrations.


4. Examples
-----------

ACG Integration Team
    |
    +--> Payment Gateway
    +--> ACG-specific integrations
    +--> Customized business integrations


Application Integration Team
    |
    +--> Address Sourcing
    +--> Other application integrations
    +--> External/application-level integrations


5. Key Difference
-----------------

ACG Integration Team
→ Focuses on integrations specific to ACG.

Application Integration Team
→ Focuses on application-level integrations and related
  integration support.


6. KT Takeaway
--------------

The ACG Integration Team handles ACG-specific and customized
integrations, while the Application Integration Team handles
application-level integrations and supporting services.

Example:

ACG-specific requirement
        ↓
ACG Integration Team
        ↓
